    <string name="wizard_s3_btn_gen_qr">Generate Deployment QR Code</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_header">Step 3: Wake Up Hidden Scanner</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_step1">【Step 1: Tap 6 Times】Tap quickly 6 times on any blank space of the \"Hello / Welcome\" screen on the old phone to activate the camera.</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_step2">【Step 2: Connect Wi-Fi】If the old phone prompts \"Wi-Fi connection needed to download barcode reader\", connect to Wi-Fi on the old phone (required by Android to download the Google scanning module).</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_step3">【Step 3: Scan QR Code】Once downloaded, the old phone camera will open automatically. Aim it at the QR code below to scan.</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_req_ts_key">Requesting Auth Key from Tailscale…</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_qr_desc">Deployment QR Code</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_qr_error">Generation Failed: %1$s</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_btn_retry">Retry</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_qr_placeholder">(Deployment QR Code)</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_faq_header">💡 Helpful Tips &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_faq1">• Why does the old phone ask to connect Wi-Fi after tapping 6 times?\nThis is standard Android behavior! After factory reset, the old phone does not have the barcode module preloaded. After connecting Wi-Fi, Google will automatically download it in 3~5 seconds and open the camera.</string>
    <string name="wizard_s4_faq2">• Tapping 6 times has no response?\nMake sure to tap 6 times rapidly (2~3 taps per second) on the blank empty area above the \"Hello / Welcome\" text.</string>

